{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition","id":1320575,"title":"Dinosaurs in Exalted 3rd Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-06-24T14:13:18-07:00","id":1320575,"title":"Dinosaurs in Exalted 3rd Edition","content":"Given that the writers of Exalted have given them different names to reflect the cultures that encounter them in Creation, identifying exactly which creatures are what we would know as dinosaurs can be a little tricky, but I think I have the start of a list for these primal beasts (and how many dots of the Familiar Merit I feel players would need to get them).<br /> <br /> From the Exalted 3E Core:<br /> <br /> Claw Strider (Raptors) 2 Dots<br /> Ox-Dragon (Triceratops) 3 Dots<br /> Raiton (Archaeopteryx) 1 Dot<br /> Siege Lizard (Stegosaurus) 3 Dots<br /> Tyrant Lizard (Tyrannosaurus Rex) 3 Dots<br /> <br /> From the Lunar Backer Access Manuscript:<br /> <br /> Iron-Skull Devil (Pachycephalosaurus) 2 Dots<br /> Shieldback Lizard (Ankylosaurus) 3 Dots<br /> Thunder Lizard (Brontosaurus) 3 Dots<br /> <br /> From Hundred Devils Night Parade<br /> <br /> Sky Titan (Quetzalcoatlus) 3 Dots<br /> <br /> I was originally going to incluse the Pestletail as well as its description was initially similar to the ankylosaurus, but upon further research of these dinosaurs, it became apparent that they didn't have turtle-like shells. It is still possible that these are a dinosaur species... I just can't identify which one (there are a lot to sort through), so until I am sure they are one (the description doesn't actually say if they are reptilian, just that they have a bony shell like a turtle or armadillo), I am not going to include them.<br /> <br /> For the Familiar dot values, I based it mostly on size and how they would stack up against other large predators and other animals. The ones that had Legendary Size would be clearly 3 Dot Familiars, while the two smaller examples (Claw Striders and Iron-Skull Devils) are more man-sized and as dangerous as a tiger or lion (given the vague guidelines provided).<br /> <br /> Now I know this far from a comprehensive list... just a list of the ones that I have stats for (and I may have missed some in the main books). This doesn't include the exclusive digital content that may be available on DrivethruRPG... as I don't have that content at this time (been hoping they will gather this content into an informal collection and provide a PoD option).<br /> <br /> If anyone wants to add to this or to tell me what I have missed, feel free to do so, but I ask we limit things to Official 3E content (no home-brews in other words).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":2243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","user":"Shadowstripe","date":". 10-07-2019, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T14:24:13-07:00","id":1320576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition#post1320575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was originally going to incluse the Pestletail as well as its description was initially similar to the ankylosaurus, but upon further research of these dinosaurs, it became apparent that they didn't have turtle-like shells. It is still possible that these are a dinosaur species... I just can't identify which one</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on the pestletail's description in the core, I think they're supposed to be <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glyptodont\" target=\"_blank\">glyptodonts</a>, which are mammals, not dinosaurs. I had made the same assumption, that they were ankylosaurs, until the Shieldback Lizard in Lunars came out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T14:37:50-07:00","id":1320577,"title":"","content":"Yeah... that does seem to match the description provided for Pestletails better. There have been so many unusual species throughout Earth's history that it can be hard to be sure which ones the writers are using since they don't provide the name we would know it as... only what the cultures of Creation would call them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T16:17:27-07:00","id":1320604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1320577#post1320577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... that does seem to match the description provided for Pestletails better. There have been so many unusual species throughout Earth's history that it can be hard to be sure which ones the writers are using since they don't provide the name we would know it as... only what the cultures of Creation would call them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, it's good to remember Creation is full of the awesome mammal megafauna that came up much after the dinossaurs and almost up to the our own contemporary age.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that considering how magic, spirits and the Wyld can make some thing wonky, it's perfectly possible to insert some species that never were - because who's to say a lion, tiger, jaguar or leopard is a &quot;more appropriate&quot; Great Cat&quot; for Creation than smilodons, snow lions, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panthera_hybrid\" target=\"_blank\">viable ligers &amp; etc</a>, or any weird variation of the previous, just a Lore roll or two away of one's game? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-24-2019, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T16:33:23-07:00","id":1320605,"title":"","content":"Another one to add to the list is actually the raiton, I think. Despite the name, it's <i>not</i> a raven, though it fills a similar cultural niche. Based on the description (&quot;small, black-feathered reptiles [with] clawed wings and a beak full of small, sharp teeth.&quot;), I'd guess they're supposed to be <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archaeopteryx\" target=\"_blank\">archaeopteryx</a> or something similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T16:46:10-07:00","id":1320608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1320604#post1320604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's good to remember Creation is full of the awesome mammal megafauna that came up much after the dinossaurs and almost up to the our own contemporary age.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that considering how magic, spirits and the Wyld can make some thing wonky, it's perfectly possible to insert some species that never were - because who's to say a lion, tiger, jaguar or leopard is a &quot;more appropriate&quot; Great Cat&quot; for Creation than smilodons, snow lions, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panthera_hybrid\" target=\"_blank\">viable ligers &amp; etc</a>, or any weird variation of the previous, just a Lore roll or two away of one's game? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget the effect that a Randy Lunar can cause to the ecosystem - cross breeds that breed true because a Lunar was one of the parents.<br /> <br /> Sadly, I haven't read 3rd (It took so long for the kickstarter, I got married and had a child, so stopped having time)<br /> But a couple of dinosaurs I remember from 1-2nd<br /> <br /> Pelagic Dragon (Plesiosaur)<br /> Sea Dragon (Mosasaur)<br /> Austrech is a Terror Bird, like the glyptodaunt, it's a later era magafauna<br /> <br /> River Dragon is a bit like a prehistoric Crocodile, which is Era appropriate, but not strictly a Dinosaur, similar to Siaka that are representative of (small) Megalodons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16927,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","user":"Illithid","date":". 06-24-2019, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T17:02:54-07:00","id":1320611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1320608#post1320608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are River Dragons explicitly in 3rd Ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they're in the Core, pp. 571-572. I think the river dragon is supposed to be a <i>really big</i> crocodilian, rather than a dinosaur <i>per se</i>, though. Something like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarcosuchus\" target=\"_blank\">sarcosuchus</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T17:23:33-07:00","id":1320615,"title":"","content":"I think that the river dragon may have just ended up where it was because it was appealing to the creators. I recall hearing that it doesn't really correspond to any particular prehistoric reptile, and in any case, it probably wouldn't be a dinosaur. They were overwhelmingly land-dwellers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition#post1320575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the writers of Exalted have given them different names to reflect the cultures that encounter them in Creation, identifying exactly which creatures are what we would know as dinosaurs can be a little tricky, but I think I have the start of a list for these primal beasts (and how many dots of the Familiar Merit I feel players would need to get them).<br /> <br /> From the Exalted 3E Core:<br /> <br /> Claw Strider (Velociraptor) 2 Dots</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Utahraptor</i>, actually. <i>Velociraptor</i> would have been not much bigger than a chicken, which is far under the description of the claw strider across editions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ox-Dragon (Triceratops) 3 Dots<br /> Siege Lizard (Stegosaurus) 3 Dots<br /> Tyrant Lizard (Tyrannosaurus Rex) 3 Dots<br /> <br /> From the Lunar Backer Access Manuscript:<br /> <br /> Iron-Skull Devil (Pachycephalosaurus) 2 Dots<br /> Shieldback Lizard (Ankylosaurus) 3 Dots<br /> Thunder Lizard (Brontosaurus) 3 Dots<br /> <br /> I was originally going to incluse the Pestletail as well as its description was initially similar to the ankylosaurus, but upon further research of these dinosaurs, it became apparent that they didn't have turtle-like shells. It is still possible that these are a dinosaur species... I just can't identify which one (there are a lot to sort through), so until I am sure they are one (the description doesn't actually say if they are reptilian, just that they have a bony shell like a turtle or armadillo), I am not going to include them.<br /> <br /> For the Familiar dot values, I based it mostly on size and how they would stack up against other large predators and other animals. The ones that had Legendary Size would be clearly 3 Dot Familiars, while the two smaller examples (Claw Striders and Iron-Skull Devils) are more man-sized and as dangerous as a tiger or lion (given the vague guidelines provided). </div> </div> </div>Those are both a good deal larger than human size, or even a big cat, even if they aren't legendary sized. They are more on par with the larger ranges of modern equines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T17:53:56-07:00","id":1320625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1320608#post1320608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget the effect that a Randy Lunar can cause to the ecosystem - cross breeds that breed true because a Lunar was one of the parents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm...<br /> <br /> I don't think any Edition has actually attributed Lunars with a native capacity to breed with animals in any shape besides one that is already compatible. I mean, strictly speaking, it wasn't until late Second Edition when cross-breeding animal and human traits became something that they could do outside of the Wyld, and their capacity to do so in the Wyld was never really distinct. Rocks and lions can make babies in the Wyld.<br /> <br /> Certainly not in this Edition, when the beastfolk children of Lunars are most likely to come from people having sex with Lunars in their hybrid bodies.<br /> <br /> I suppose that it's not strictly beyond the scope of a Lunar narrative to employ some kind of odd magic to enable such unions but... ehh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Thunder Lizard (Brontosaurus)</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Wellll\u2026<br /> <br /> {takes a second to look into it}<br /> <br /> Ah dang, they went and made Brontosaurus the name for an actual genus a few years back? Shiiit, I grew up with the information that it was an outdated and erroneous term for what had become called brachiosaurus and Apatosaurus. That's going to take some adjustment.<br /> <br /> Paleontology is freaking weird.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T20:45:05-07:00","id":1320651,"title":"","content":"Pestletails are indeed glyptodons. I think they were a backer reward choice, even.<br /> <br /> Despite what one would think at first, angler lizards are <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tanystropheus\" target=\"_blank\">Tanystropheus</a>, which surprsiingly are not dinosaurs despite their looks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T21:35:49-07:00","id":1320658,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar16927_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"16927\" data-vbnamecard=\"16927\">Illithid</a>, that it technically wasn't a dinosaur yet lived at the same time is the reason I didn't include it in this list... a lot of creatures existed during the age of the dinosaurs that weren't actually dinosaurs does make it harder to come up with a clear list.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a>, I do know that the Claw Strider and Iron Skull Devil are still more massive than a human, they are more along the human-scale than most the others presented, thus I felt they didn't quite merit the full 3 Dot familiar status... and over all they would be roughly seen as as much of a threat as any other large predator or large herbivore would be given the broad parameters for familiar levels. Besides... Horses are seen as 2 Dot familiars anyways. I must also coment that you must know of some rather large chickens to compare valociraptors to their size... they are closer to the size of a turkey now that I have seen a more accurate picture of them compared to humans (movies really do like playing loose with the actual creatures they are presenting... which I admit I was initially basing my comparison off of).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a>, yeah... I was surprised by that too...but then the auto-correct my computer uses doesn't accept the name I originally put as valid (probably because I misspelled it) and I didn't realize it was changed until you mentioned it now.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1533_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1533\" data-vbnamecard=\"1533\">Kelly Pedersen</a>, without a clear picture of what a Raiton looks like, I am reluctant to claim it as an archaeopteryx despite the similarities in general description... though if we do get such a picture (even one from a previous edition) I would be inclined to agree that it has a place here. This really is a problem with the writers deciding which Earth animals to give new names to and which to keep... it makes it very difficult to know for sure which animals are actually in the setting.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar353_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"353\" data-vbnamecard=\"353\">Blaque</a>, hence the reason I chose not to include them on the list... the first because it clearly isn't a dinosaur... and the other because, despite its appearance, it technically wasn't one either.<br /> <br /> In case people are wondering why I included the reference as to how many dots of familiar each would likely be worth... it is, in part, for the Heart's Blood Merit for Lunars. Each dot can give the Lunar a number of forms roughly equivalent to various Familiar ratings. One Dot of Heart's Blood provides roughly 6 shapes equivalent to a 1 Dot familiar, about 3 shapes equal to a 2 Dot familiar or 1 shape on par with a 3 Dot familiar (okay... this is a little looser interpretation, but a fair one I think as I see no reason to restrict the choice of animals to a single direction given how far ranging Lunars can be... especially when being guided by other Lunars).<br /> <br /> The other reason is because I am creating a Lunar Exalt with a Dinosaur Spirit Shape who will be limiting the other forms he takes to these primal beasts, seeing them as Creations mightiest beasts. I am thinking he came from a tribe that venerated these beasts almost like Gods... and may have been one of the only cultures that actually tamed any of them. I am thinking that the tribe may have had its origin around the fall of Rathess during the Great Contagion, with their tales of living with the Dragon-Kings slowly blending with the mighty saurians over the centuries. I can't remember the name of the Southern Jungle Goddess from the 2nd Ed books (and don't have access to them to look it up), but the one I am thinking of did have some reptilian features... and did her best not to get dragged into the petty squabble her sibling forest Gods (and their mortal followers) had to the North. I'm thinking his tribe venerated her as their patron, and in turn let them tame some of these creatures to help them survive where these giants walked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T00:05:56-07:00","id":1320674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1320608#post1320608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget the effect that a Randy Lunar can cause to the ecosystem - cross breeds that breed true because a Lunar was one of the parents.<br /> <br /> Sadly, I haven't read 3rd (It took so long for the kickstarter, I got married and had a child, so stopped having time)<br /> But a couple of dinosaurs I remember from 1-2nd<br /> <br /> Pelagic Dragon (Plesiosaur)<br /> Sea Dragon (Mosasaur)<br /> Austrech is a Terror Bird, like the glyptodaunt, it's a later era magafauna<br /> <br /> River Dragon is a bit like a prehistoric Crocodile, which is Era appropriate, but not strictly a Dinosaur, similar to Siaka that are representative of (small) Megalodons</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> getting anal here, but neither Plesiosaurs nor mosasaurs are dinosaurs, though they lived at the same time. But I will give you extra credit for calling a terror bird a dinosaur, since that's what birds are<br /> <br /> And on the subject of river dragons, I thought those would be something like kronosaurus, since I thought they were to be fully aquatic while sarcosuchus being a crocodile can come on land.<br /> <br /> On a side note, the Sci-show channel on Youtube just had an episode on <a href=\"https://youtu.be/vh2wRYQPCPk\" target=\"_blank\">extinct crocodiles</a>. Some would make awesome Lunar forms, and is fun to check out in any case","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 06-25-2019, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T00:40:14-07:00","id":1320678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1320625#post1320625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly not in this Edition, when the beastfolk children of Lunars are most likely to come from people having sex with Lunars in their hybrid bodies.<br /> <br /> I suppose that it's not strictly beyond the scope of a Lunar narrative to employ some kind of odd magic to enable such unions but... ehh.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar's 2nd ed</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar Exalts have the ability to pass on both the bestial traits of a shape that they wear, and the mystic power that Luna has granted them, or sometimes both to the same offspring.<br /> <br /> To breed beastman, in the absence of charms, the Lunar exalt must engage is a cross-species coupling. It should be noted that vast differences in size between mates are not feasible, and that many beastman births are dangerous to the mother. In addition, the Lunar must meet one of the following criteria:<br /> The coupling takes place in the Bordermarches or deeper in the Wyld.<br /> The Lunar has essence 4+.<br /> A half-caste child may be the result of any Lunar coupling provided at least one parent is human at the time of the act. Additionally the Lunar must have essence 4, though having 3+ dots of cult lowers this requirement by one as does living within the influence of an uncapped demense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, it just says cross-species coupling. It never explicitly says animal-human, implying animal-animal is possible. Probably frowned upon due to the Chimera connotations. But Possible.<br /> I haven't read the manuscript for Lunars 3rd ed though if it's worded too differently.<br /> <br /> Also, when it comes to descriptions, most of the depictions of Dinos are highly speculative, so it could be &quot;similar enough&quot; and still be more real than our current images.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16927,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","user":"Illithid","date":". 06-25-2019, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T01:57:05-07:00","id":1320687,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's from last edition's lunars. They shook things up a bit with Fangs At The Gate.<br /> <br /> Lunars <i>can</i> just give animals the traits of other animals with a charm now. So hybrids are still viable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T02:19:28-07:00","id":1320695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1320674#post1320674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And on the subject of river dragons, I thought those would be something like kronosaurus, since I thought they were to be fully aquatic while sarcosuchus being a crocodile can come on land.</div> </div> </div> </div>River dragons can go onto land, however - note their Lunge From the Depths ability, which is explicitly a charge from the water at an enemy on land. To me, it sounds like the river dragon is aquatic the way a Nile or saltwater crocodile is: water is their primary habitat, but you <i>absolutely</i> aren't safe anywhere a short run away from water. They'll just drag you back to the water to eat you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T02:24:24-07:00","id":1320697,"title":"","content":"the current description does, but earlier editions sounded more like a fully aquatic animal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T03:08:04-07:00","id":1320702,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s a strong argument to be made for the Austrech here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T03:37:48-07:00","id":1320704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1320678#post1320678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read the manuscript for Lunars 3rd ed though if it's worded too differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have, and it's worded the way I said it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The children who inherit supernatural are called Moon-Touched now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T03:52:35-07:00","id":1320708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1320608#post1320608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget the effect that a Randy Lunar can cause to the ecosystem - cross breeds that breed true because a Lunar was one of the parents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly possible, but i try to focus first in those methods that are not exalt-dependent or specific first.<br /> <br /> That and Creation's &quot;vanilla weirdness&quot; being enough to allow for not only <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panthera_hybrid\" target=\"_blank\">panthera hybrid</a> variants as viable species of their own but even more idiosyncratic crossbreeds. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1320702#post1320702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s a strong argument to be made for the Austrech here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They would be something akin to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moa\" target=\"_blank\">Moas</a>, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-25-2019, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T06:03:47-07:00","id":1320730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1320708#post1320708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would be something akin to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moa\" target=\"_blank\">Moas</a>, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they're birds of a different feather. Moa were herbivorous. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phorusrhacidae\" target=\"_blank\">Phorusrhacidae</a> were carnivorous; they earned the nickname Terror Birds quite honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 06-25-2019, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T09:11:18-07:00","id":1320764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1320730#post1320730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they're birds of a different feather. Moa were herbivorous. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phorusrhacidae\" target=\"_blank\">Phorusrhacidae</a> were carnivorous; they earned the nickname Terror Birds quite honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My bad, i do have a bad habit of mixing them up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T10:06:03-07:00","id":1320777,"title":"","content":"Raitons are absolutely archeopterixes, though there's one illustration in the 2nd edition core that just made them ravens with visible fangs sticking out of the beak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T12:35:05-07:00","id":1320812,"title":"","content":"Well, with that said, I have added Raitons to the list as a 1 Dot Familiar... do to their small size and tendency to flee threats rather than fight. Of course a flock of them would likely be more dangerous, but individually I think they rate more as this than as a typical 2 Dot Familiar. I wonder if Mospids from the earlier editions would likely use similar stats and be seen as similar dinosaur-like avian.<br /> <br /> Okay... now trying to think of the name of the Eastern Goddess of Jungles is really starting to become an obsession of mine. Why did I have to leave my 2nd Edition books in storage when I moved? Oh well... hindsight is 20/20 and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T15:11:44-07:00","id":1320836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1320697#post1320697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the current description does, but earlier editions sounded more like a fully aquatic animal</div> </div> </div> </div>It was always weird since as noted, they probably aren't based on a real megafauna originally, but in later books (<b>Savage Seas </b>notably) <i>did</i> make it so they were related to sea dragons (which were obviously mososaurs). I have kind of always chalked this up to the authors being on a good track (I like most megafauna in Creation just being &quot;Classical person's account of exotic creature gone wild&quot;) but also not knowing their biology and not realizing there weren't really many if any inland mososaurs and something like that isn't common in rivers. This has then gotten retained in the art for htem in 3e a bit.<br /> <br /> My headcanon is they're Saurosuchus since giant scary-ass crocodiles are cool, and it fits the right biolotical niche I would expect for a semi-aquatic predatory river reptile than something with flippers usually would","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T15:58:28-07:00","id":1320843,"title":"","content":"In a discussion of one of the most recent Adversaries of the Righteous the devs (I think Vance) did mention that river dragons, at least in 3E, are explicitly enormous crocodiles/alligators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T18:19:34-07:00","id":1320868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1320836#post1320836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My headcanon is they're Saurosuchus since giant scary-ass crocodiles are cool, and it fits the right biolotical niche I would expect for a semi-aquatic predatory river reptile than something with flippers usually would</div> </div> </div> </div>Sarcosuchus. Saurosuchus wasn't a crocodile, but from a related family that was fully terrestrial.<br /> <br /> And would fit great in Creation too. Would love to see people taminf and riding that, or ticinosuchus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T19:08:33-07:00","id":1320874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1320843#post1320843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a discussion of one of the most recent Adversaries of the Righteous the devs (I think Vance) did mention that river dragons, at least in 3E, are explicitly enormous crocodiles/alligators.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup they do have that crocostimpy death roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T22:16:15-07:00","id":1320894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1320874#post1320874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup they do have that crocostimpy death roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deathrolls, at least in game media, seem to be at some point were decided as the signature move of big-ol'crocs./<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T22:17:23-07:00","id":1320895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1320868#post1320868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sarcosuchus. Saurosuchus wasn't a crocodile, but from a related family that was fully terrestrial.<br /> <br /> And would fit great in Creation too. Would love to see people taminf and riding that, or ticinosuchus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, they're a crocodiliomorph (modern crocodiles and other croc-shaped relatives). Close, but not quite and all that. Still more closer to modern crocs than really anything else though.<br /> <br /> Fun fact to me though is how crocs in general are more closely related to birds and idnos than other reptiles, including a lot of the aquatic ones back in the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T23:48:18-07:00","id":1321113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1320777#post1320777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raitons are absolutely archeopterixes, though there's one illustration in the 2nd edition core that just made them ravens with visible fangs sticking out of the beak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now we know why it was weeping and cast-aside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T00:20:32-07:00","id":1321125,"title":"","content":"what ever happened to mospids? did they get replaced by raitons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T00:29:56-07:00","id":1321126,"title":"","content":"Feathered Reptile does sound like a dinosaur/ scaled bird","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T01:33:13-07:00","id":1321132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1321125#post1321125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what ever happened to mospids?</div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microraptor\" target=\"_blank\">microraptors</a> have been briefly name-dropped in several places, but no description or writeup so far.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T02:10:04-07:00","id":1321135,"title":"","content":"this thread has me browsing articles on archosaurs now, and found this:<br /> <br /> [img]<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erythrosuchus\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erythrosuchus</a>[/img]<br /> <br /> we need this in Creation somewhere","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T08:42:40-07:00","id":1321174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1321125#post1321125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what ever happened to mospids? did they get replaced by raitons?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mospids appear to still exist - the core book mentions them once, and the Lunars manuscript does twice. Their 2e writeup doesn't have anything very distinctive going on, so for 3e stats, I'd just take the eagle stats from the corebook straight up. The eagle writeup even mentions that mospids are competitors!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T12:25:18-07:00","id":1321218,"title":"","content":"Doing a bit of digging, looks like Mospids were among the critters that got axed from the 3E core, which could very well mean we could see them again in Hundred Devils or other supplement. From what I can find the Eagle splat is pretty comparable, though, so decent placeholder. (And redundance is a possible reason our lovely snake birds got axed in the first place)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T17:09:20-07:00","id":1321280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1321135#post1321135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this thread has me browsing articles on archosaurs now, and found this:<br /> <br /> [img]<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erythrosuchus\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erythrosuchus</a>[/img]<br /> <br /> we need this in Creation somewhere</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at the face on that, It belongs in Creation, or a Kaiju movie","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T22:35:01-07:00","id":1321331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition#post1320575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the writers of Exalted have given them different names to reflect the cultures that encounter them in Creation, identifying exactly which creatures are what we would know as dinosaurs can be a little tricky, but I think I have the start of a list for these primal beasts (and how many dots of the Familiar Merit I feel players would need to get them).<br /> If anyone wants to add to this or to tell me what I have missed, feel free to do so, but I ask we limit things to Official 3E content (no home-brews in other words).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's second hand now, but the quoted section below may be handy. I got it from Reddit<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Quoting Stephen Lea Sheppard from the official forums:<br /> <br /> The angler lizard is a Tanystropheus.<br /> The armored terror is a Dunkelosteus.<br /> The benthic knifetooth is an up-sized and up-fierced frilled shark.<br /> The boar-tusk crocodile is a a Kaprosuchus.<br /> The bunyip is a Diprotodon.<br /> The claw strider is a Deinonychus.<br /> The death moa It's a Bullockornis. Thank you, Vance.<br /> The emperor sloth is a Megatherium.<br /> The hellboar... It's an Entelodont.<br /> The ox-dragon is a Triceratops or some other ceratopsid, yeah. <br /> The pestletail is a Glyptodont, and therefore a mammal and not a turtle. The stats would work for an ankylosaurus, though.<br /> The quoll-lion is a marsupial lion.<br /> The raiton is an Archeopteryx.<br /> The river-dragon is from Exalted 1e and may or may not correspond to any particular bit of prehistoric megafauna.<br /> The siege lizard is a Stegosaurus.<br /> The tyrant lizard is, indeed, T. rex.<br /> The yeddim is an original Exalted animal but seems to most closely resemble Paraceratherium. Or maybe some descendent of Paraceratherium after thousands of years of domestication by god-heroes.<br /> Most of these were chosen by backers who purchased the &quot;Choose an example of prehistoric megafauna for us to put in the book&quot; reward tier. I was really, really hoping someone would choose Quetzalcoatlus northropi, but nobody did, alas. </div> </div> </div>And someone suggested that the Hybroc was a Quetzalcoatlus","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T23:21:12-07:00","id":1321340,"title":"","content":"question: do the tyrant lizard stats (and merits and such) need adjusted to make say an allosaur or saurophaganax? or are they generic enough to use as is for any large theropod <br /> <br /> I wanted to make a lunar Saurophaganax* and wondering about that<br /> <br /> *and that would be his name too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T23:40:44-07:00","id":1321346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1321340#post1321340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">question: do the tyrant lizard stats (and merits and such) need adjusted to make say an allosaur or saurophaganax? or are they generic enough to use as is for any large theropod<br /> <br /> I wanted to make a lunar Saurophaganax* and wondering about that<br /> <br /> *and that would be his name too</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'd say you'd be fine. If you wanted to reflect them being smaller just knock a few dice off its pools and maybe a few health levels","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","user":"SamuraiMujuru","date":". 06-28-2019, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T23:46:16-07:00","id":1321347,"title":"","content":"I'm joining a friend of mine hoping we get a therizinosaurus some day","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T23:57:29-07:00","id":1321350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1321340#post1321340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">question: do the tyrant lizard stats (and merits and such) need adjusted to make say an allosaur or saurophaganax? or are they generic enough to use as is for any large theropod</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, if I was using them as antagonists, I'd probably dial back the tyrant lizard stats a bit. Maybe not remove legendary size, but knock a health level or two off most steps of their track, dial back their damage a point or two, that kind of thing. Tyrant lizards are supposed to be the Top Dog (top dinosaur?), so it makes sense other large theropod predators aren't <i>quite</i> as impressive, and allosaurus and saurophaganax are both smaller than t-rexes, according to modern reconstructions. The mass difference is particularly notable - according to Wikipedia, at least, allosaurus is estimated to have weighed about 2.5 tons, compared to 9.3 tons for t-rex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T13:00:00-07:00","id":1321421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1321347#post1321347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm joining a friend of mine hoping we get a therizinosaurus some day</div> </div> </div> </div>You could fudge things a bit with giant sloths and anteaters, if they show up first. Provided, of course, they're giant enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T21:57:35-07:00","id":1321460,"title":"","content":"we have giant sloths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T22:30:03-07:00","id":1321461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1321460#post1321460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">we have giant sloths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emperor Sloth to be precise. (Ex3 core, pgs 563-4)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T01:11:18-07:00","id":1321476,"title":"","content":"You know, in conversations such as this, I'm surprised that Iguanodon hardly ever seems to come up. They were one of the first I learned about when I started getting into dinosaurs, and I'd think they would be more popular with their easy to remember name and distinctive physical feature, with how it can be deployed defensively.<br /> <br /> Heck, they started in a Disney movie, and that's often supposed to cement one's status as a pop culture icon.<br /> <br /> But no, there's hardly any love for the big cows with the neck-stabbing murder thumbs.<br /> <br /> I wonder what Iguanodon would be called in Creation...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T01:28:42-07:00","id":1321479,"title":"","content":"actially, duckbills aren't mentioned either. Iguanadons I just figured were too mundane. but duckbills should be unique enough with the crests to get some attention.<br /> <br /> and on that note, what about Dicynodonts? I know not dinosaurs, though some in the kannemeyerform family did get to sizes rivaling rhinos and elephants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T06:55:49-07:00","id":1321710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1321476#post1321476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, in conversations such as this, I'm surprised that Iguanodon hardly ever seems to come up. They were one of the first I learned about when I started getting into dinosaurs, and I'd think they would be more popular with their easy to remember name and distinctive physical feature, with how it can be deployed defensively.<br /> <br /> Heck, they started in a Disney movie, and that's often supposed to cement one's status as a pop culture icon.<br /> <br /> But no, there's hardly any love for the big cows with the neck-stabbing murder thumbs.<br /> <br /> I wonder what Iguanodon would be called in Creation...</div> </div> </div> </div>Going off other naming schemes, Dagger-hand Lizard maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T07:27:40-07:00","id":1321717,"title":"","content":"As I've been watching this thread (because fuck yeah, dinosaurs!) I noticed I've been googling a bunch of the names. Got half a mind to cobble together a document of what creature to what megafauna guide with reference pictures and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T08:46:48-07:00","id":1321730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1321476#post1321476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, in conversations such as this, I'm surprised that Iguanodon hardly ever seems to come up. They were one of the first I learned about when I started getting into dinosaurs, and I'd think they would be more popular with their easy to remember name and distinctive physical feature, with how it can be deployed defensively.<br /> <br /> Heck, they started in a Disney movie, and that's often supposed to cement one's status as a pop culture icon.<br /> <br /> But no, there's hardly any love for the big cows with the neck-stabbing murder thumbs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess most of the love goes for <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brontosaurus\" target=\"_blank\">brontos</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triceratops\" target=\"_blank\">triceratops</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stegosaurus\" target=\"_blank\">stegosaurs</a> and related or similar species.<br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, though not really dinosaurs - and in fact much older than most dino families - i'm a bit partial to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dimetrodon\" target=\"_blank\">dimetrodons</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T08:56:09-07:00","id":1321732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1321717#post1321717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I've been watching this thread (because fuck yeah, dinosaurs!) I noticed I've been googling a bunch of the names. Got half a mind to cobble together a document of what creature to what megafauna guide with reference pictures and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually been thinking of something similar. I actually went through teh books and dug about to find what would be the total list of things, based on SLS' post and some other digging. The start would probably be this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> COREBOOK<br /> Angler Lizard - Tanystropheus<br /> Armored Terror - Dunkleosteus<br /> Benthic Knifetooth - Scaled-up and meaner frilled shark<br /> Boar-Tusk Crocodile - Kaprosuchus<br /> Bunyip - Diprotodon<br /> Clawstrider - A Jurassic Park-scaled manoraptor<br /> Death Moa - Bullockornis<br /> Emperor Sloth - Megatherium<br /> Hellboar - Entelodont<br /> Ox-Dragon - Triceratops<br /> Pestletail - Glyptodont<br /> Quoll-Lion - Thylacoleo carnifex<br /> Raiton - Archeopteryx<br /> River Dragon - Unknown, potentially Saurosuchus imperator<br /> Siege Lizard - Stegosaurus<br /> Tyrant Lizard - Tyranasaurus rex<br /> Yeddim - Unknown, potentially Paraceratherium<br /> <br /> LUNARS<br /> Iron-Skull Devil - Pachycephalosaurus<br /> Shieldback Lizard - Ankylosaur<br /> Thunder Lizard - Brontosaurus<br /> <br /> HUNDRED DEVILS NIGHT PARADE<br /> Austrech - Phorusrhacids a.k.a. terror bird<br /> Giant Constrictor - Titanoboa </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T09:49:20-07:00","id":1321744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1321732#post1321732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've actually been thinking of something similar. I actually went through teh books and dug about to find what would be the total list of things, based on SLS' post and some other digging. The start would probably be this:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo, forgot about HDNP. Adding those to the to-do list!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T10:25:58-07:00","id":1321749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1321476#post1321476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, in conversations such as this, I'm surprised that Iguanodon hardly ever seems to come up. They were one of the first I learned about when I started getting into dinosaurs, and I'd think they would be more popular with their easy to remember name and distinctive physical feature, with how it can be deployed defensively.<br /> <br /> Heck, they started in a Disney movie, and that's often supposed to cement one's status as a pop culture icon.<br /> <br /> But no, there's hardly any love for the big cows with the neck-stabbing murder thumbs.<br /> <br /> I wonder what Iguanodon would be called in Creation...</div> </div> </div> </div>Weirdly I learned more about Iguanodon's on my 1-week trip to London museums than I did in all my years growing up in the US. Weird cultural divide when it comes to favored dinosaurs. I agree, they should definitely be more of a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T20:07:06-07:00","id":1322143,"title":"","content":"Hiya everybody! I did a thing! Obviously, it's not perfect, but hopefully it'll be handy!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1Ra0yMjGhatuuTzNo6mSnZvvicBJK4YkCprZD-aP8zFE\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1Ra0yMjGhatuuTzNo6mSnZvvicBJK4YkCprZD-aP8zFE\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1Ra0yMjGhatuuTzNo6mSnZvvicBJK4YkCprZD-aP8zFE\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/open?id=1Ra0yMjGhatuuTzNo6mSnZvvicBJK4YkCprZD-aP8zFE </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b>