"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-01T03:36:40-07:00","id":1328704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1325868#post1325868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">doing more research for fun (I have no life), and found these images of what they think the armored terror actually looked like:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://qph.fs.quoracdn.net/main-qimg-6f9b1076e0683c11c222cfc806bf8170\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/c4045bc8-87ce-4c02-96c6-0cda7e3e652d/d9l0elw-ef69d0fb-bc9c-452a-b81d-fa9aabaf32e8.png/v1/fill/w_1778,h_449,strp/dunkleosteus_terrelli_by_spinoinwonderland_d9l0elw-pre.png?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..ahuHJYZLBBHuaFDdblXCkE5kSkKy8nzu9C9ze60DkAw\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> yup. instead of the armor and toothplates on the outside, it had skin and lips on it like a real animal</div> </div> </div> </div>The first of those is accompanying some random guy on the Internet making an argument saying that the Dunkleosteus probably had lips, and the other is a Deviantart picture in which the artist days that they decided to give it lips.<br /> <br /> Do you have a reference from an actual paleontologist asserting that it may have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-01T08:48:15-07:00","id":1328736,"title":"","content":"Did some digging and couldn't find anything definitive in the literature but not on campus to read some of them so can't be sure.<br /> <br /> There is talk that the sheers part of its mouth might still have been exposed, much like a parrot fish. (You can look those up on Google Images, they can be rather pretty.)<br /> <br /> One comrpomise reconstruction I saw was this, where most of the animal is covered in skin save the sheers, which are exposed:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://phys.org/newman/gfx/news/hires/2012/theevolution.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://phys.org/newman/gfx/news/hires/2012/theevolution.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://phys.org/newman/gfx/news/hires/2012/theevolution.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://phys.org/newman/gfx/news/hires/2012/theevolution.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-01T12:53:36-07:00","id":1328774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1328611#post1328611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although it is, in spirit, <i>Q. northropi</i>, the sky titan is named after <i>Aerotitan sudamericanus</i>, another azhdarchid with a name that better fits Exalted\u2019s standard for naming its dinosaurs\u2014we didn\u2019t want to call it a feathered serpent because it\u2019s not a serpent and doesn\u2019t have feathers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something went wrong with that then, because the text of HDNP does say they have feathers (though the art doesn't seem to have them).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hundred Devils Night Parade</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their feathers, arrayed in a violent spray of colors, form fearsome patterns when their wings unfurl.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Let us take men and give them the favor of the gods and use them as our champions against the Primordials, that we might overthrow them and play for ourselves the Games of Divinity.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2272-senresk","name":"senresk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-01T13:49:57-07:00","id":1328788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>senresk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1320575-dinosaurs-in-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1328774#post1328774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something went wrong with that then, because the text of HDNP does say they have feathers (though the art doesn't seem to have them).<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As I noted, pterosaurs migh have actually had feathers afterall:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.newscientist.com/article/2188405-stunning-fossils-show-pterosaurs-had-primitive-feathers-like-dinosaurs/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://images.newscientist.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/17133342/pterosaur.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.newscientist.com/article/2188405-stunning-fossils-show-pterosaurs-had-primitive-feathers-like-dinosaurs/\" target=\"_blank\"> Stunning fossils show pterosaurs had primitive feathers like dinosaurs </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.newscientist.com/article/2188405-stunning-fossils-show-pterosaurs-had-primitive-feathers-like-dinosaurs/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.newscientist.com/article/2188405-stunning-fossils-show-pterosaurs-had-primitive-feathers-like-dinosaurs/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> When dinosaurs ruled the land, pterosaurs occupied the skies. Now we know they had feathers, suggesting plumage has a much deeper history than we had thought </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-01T20:50:19-07:00","id":1328870,"title":"","content":"Sky Titan/Quetzacoatlus added to the document!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1Ra0yMjGhatuuTzNo6mSnZvvicBJK4YkCprZD-aP8zFE\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_contai